# What the browser is given.
#
# Both of these are meant to be public and are compiled into the
# bundle. The URL says which project the shop talks to; the
# publishable key identifies the project, not a person. What that key
# may actually do is decided by row-level security on every table.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill them in. Without them the shop still
# runs - the catalogue is in the bundle - but nothing can be ordered
# and the admin panel has nobody to sign in.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# --------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT HERE. These belong to the Edge Functions and are set with
#   supabase secrets set NAME=value
# They must never be given a VITE_ prefix, never be committed, and
# never appear in anything the browser downloads.
#
#   R2_ACCOUNT_ID          the Cloudflare account the bucket is in
#   R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID       an R2 API token, scoped to this bucket only
#   R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY   its secret
#   R2_BUCKET              wrappedstudio-originals
#   R2_ENDPOINT            optional, if not the default S3 endpoint
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS        the sites allowed to call the functions,
#                          comma separated, e.g.
#                          https://wrappedstudio.in,http://localhost:5173
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are provided to the
# functions by Supabase itself and are not set by hand.
#
# Phase 2 will add RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET,
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET and BREVO_API_KEY to the same place.
